  "context": {
    "comparability": "Four populations, never one uniform 2000-2024 growth rate: nonbank >$3m (2000-01); nonbank >$10m (2002-06); including banks >$15m (2007-11); including banks >$20m (2012-24). Thresholds use assets, sales, or net income/loss and are nominal USD. Benchmark survey frames can also change, including 2017 and 2022. Changes are not necessarily new firms or exits.",
    "count_threshold_not_annual_sample_threshold": "The 2000 published count cutoff is $3m, not the $30m annual-reporting sample cutoff. Very small affiliates can contribute to other estimated financial totals while being excluded from published affiliate counts.",
    "geography": "United States host. Mainland China and Hong Kong UBO locations remain separate. Macau is not supplied by these count tables and is not assigned zero.",
    "ownership": "More than 50 percent foreign ownership; country of ultimate beneficial owner (UBO), not the immediate foreign parent. Counts are consolidated affiliate reporting units, not unique foreign parents, every legal company or establishments.",
    "period": "Fiscal reporting year ending in the stated calendar year, not a current-year estimate. 2024 is the latest released inward activity year as reviewed; its figures are preliminary.",
    "question": "How have majority-owned U.S. affiliates with mainland China and Hong Kong ultimate beneficial owners changed?",
    "rights": "Aggregate original government statistics and exact source references only. Raw tables and reports remain private."
  },
